# Allowlist-only .gitignore: this repo tracks exactly the shared coding-agent
# rules files and nothing else in this home directory. Ignore everything by
# default, then un-ignore only the specific paths we want tracked.
#
# NEVER `git add -A` or `git add .` in this repo — always add the exact
# allowlisted paths below. This directory holds real credentials
# (.ssh, .git-credentials, .gsutil, .pki, .config/gh/hosts.yml, .claude.json,
# .claude/projects/ transcripts, etc.) that must never enter this repo.

/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md

!/.agent-rules
!/.agent-rules/**

# Host rules for a session opened on this directory. Relative symlinks to
# .agent-rules/AGENTS.md, so they survive a clone. Cursor reads AGENTS.md;
# Claude Code reads CLAUDE.md at the project root (it has no AGENTS.md
# fallback). The absolute-path farm (~/.gemini/AGENTS.md, ~/.codex/AGENTS.md)
# is the installer's job, not git's. Claude also loads ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md
# in every session, so the root CLAUDE.md is belt-and-braces for a home
# checkout, not the only path those rules take.
!/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md

# Guard values for sessions rooted here, read by every agent's hook adapter.
!/.agent-guards.json

!/.claude
/.claude/*
!/.claude/CLAUDE.md
!/.claude/settings.json

!/.gemini
/.gemini/*
!/.gemini/GEMINI.md

# Cursor has no user-level rules file, but it does have user-level hooks.
# Track hooks.json and .cursor/.gitignore only. The nested gitignore is
# Cursor-managed between its markers and *un-ignores* session dirs
# (projects/**, plugins/**, …); our post-marker overrides in that file
# re-assert the allowlist. Do not rely on `.git/info/exclude` for this —
# nested .gitignore outranks it.
!/.cursor
/.cursor/*
!/.cursor/hooks.json
!/.cursor/.gitignore
